  "liner": {
   "body_md": "Mountain Goats performed a full 99-minute set at the Evanston SPACE on Sunday, July 2, 2023, captured in a matrix recording that blends soundboard audio with audience microphones [1]. This specific taping, identified as show 375 in the archive’s collection for the band, follows their previous archived performance at The Salt Shed on July 1, 2023 [3]. The setlist spans their discography, opening with “Liza Forever Minnelli” from *All Eternals Deck* and “Broom People” from *The Sunset Tree* before moving into tracks like “Birth of Serpents” and “Mobile” [1]. Several songs are notable for their rarity in the archive; “Counting Song for Bitter Children” marks its first appearance in 144 archived shows, while “Song for an Old Friend” returns after 200 shows and “Deuteronomy 2:10” after 94 [3]. The performance includes spoken introductions for “No Children” and “Cadaver Sniffing Dog” [1]. The set concludes with a five-song encore featuring “The Slow Parts on Death Metal Albums” and “No Children” [1]. The uploader notes that while the show was not a good time for them personally, this was unrelated to the content, and they thank Danny of the house for the soundboard patch, Brandon Eggleston for the mix, and the band for supporting livetaping [1]. A listener review of this specific recording praises the show, stating that any live show where Peter is forced to entertain the audience is a good one, and describes the band as a fount of all music knowledge [2]. The recording has been rated 5/5 by one listener [1].",
